  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "What to Ask Before Hiring a General Contractor",
    "text": "What to Ask Before Hiring a General Contractor",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Hiring a general contractor for your home project is a big decision, and asking the right questions upfront can save you a lot of trouble. Don't be shy about digging in! First, ask about their experience with projects similar to yours. Have they done kitchen or bathroom remodels, basement finishes, or other work that matches what you need? It’s also crucial to ask who will actually be on-site supervising the work day-to-day. For example, Abraham at HH Remodeling LLC is often on-site himself, which is a huge plus for hands-on management. Next, clarify how many projects they’re managing concurrently and what that means for your project's timeline. You want to understand their capacity. Communication is key, so ask about their preferred method of contact and how often you can expect updates. Also, it’s smart to inquire about their process for handling potential delays or unforeseen issues, and how they manage billing and any disagreements that might arise. Finally, always ask for proof of general liability insurance and current licensing. These questions help ensure you're hiring a competent and reliable professional who can deliver a smooth, successful project.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
